  "content": {
    "id": "v2-1a2026-p7-practice-slot-4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Sam borrows $\\$8000$ at $5\\%$ p.a. compounding annually and repays $\\$1200$ at the end of each year. Choose the recurrence relation that models the balance of the loan, $V_n$, after $n$ repayments.\n\nA. $V_n=V_{n-1}\\times0.05-1200,\\ V_0=8000$\nB. $V_n=V_{n-1}\\times1.05+1200,\\ V_0=8000$\nC. $V_n=V_{n-1}\\times1.05-1200,\\ V_0=8000$\nD. $V_n=V_{n-1}\\times1.05-1200,\\ V_0=0$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "C",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}r&=0.05\\\\V_n&=V_{n-1}(1+0.05)-1200\\\\V_n&=V_{n-1}\\times1.05-1200\\end{align*}$$\nThe repayment is subtracted, and the loan starts at $V_0=8000$. The answer is C.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": null
  },
